  {
   "id": "-Mv1Xz0OCwAJ",
   "from": "Mauricio Garnier-Villarreal",
   "author": "82889e926eb5165e",
   "date": "2020-01-28T03:33:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: Standard error (SE) of difference between two independent gains via lavaan",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The same way he did it in the post. <br></div><div><br></div><div>You use the := operator, to create this effect size, using named parameters for the mean differences and variances. <br></div><div><br></div><div>Also, notice that lavaan will estimate the variances, not standard deviations, so you will need to ask for the square root of those. Somtehing like this</div><div><br></div><div>Lets say the parameters are named as such in the lavaan model<br></div><div>- MD1 = Mean.dif<font size=\"1\">group 1</font><br></div><div>- VR1 (variance)= SD.dif<font size=\"1\">group 1</font><br></div><div>- MD2 = Mean.dif\r\n\r\n<font size=\"1\">group 2</font><br></div><div>- VR2 (variance)= SD.dif<font size=\"1\">group 2</font></div><div><br></div><div>EFFECT SIZE = [Mean.dif<font size=\"1\">group 1</font>/SD.dif<font size=\"1\">group 1</font>] − [Mean.dif\r\n\r\n<font size=\"1\">group 2</font> /SD.dif<font size=\"1\">group 2</font>] ### this translate into the define parameter EF<br></div><div>EF := (MD1/sqrt(VR1)) - (MD2/sqrt(VR2))<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br></div>On Monday, January 27, 2020 at 9:09:37 PM UTC-6, Reza Norouzian wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello all,<div><br></div><div>In <a href=\"https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/256053/variance-of-cohens-d-for-within-subjects-designs/258583#258583\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/256053/variance-of-cohens-d-for-within-subjects-designs/258583%23258583&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422446668000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Fj9GCIvnZyHPtRxdg-RUB\"><b>his post</b></a>, <a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=kuTjTlsAAAAJ&amp;hl=en\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://scholar.google.com/citations?user%3DkuTjTlsAAAAJ%26hl%3Den&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422446668000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0V0KsSwAyOmblFGXIpPPOG\">Mike Cheung</a> provides a lavaan solution to obtain SE for the effect size in pre-post experiment with one group of subjects.<div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"></span>But suppose we have two independent pre-post groups. I&#39;ve calculated an effect size for the difference between two standardized pre-post differences of two independent groups of subjects. That is:</div><div><br></div><div>EFFECT SIZE = [Mean.dif<font size=\"1\">group 1</font>/SD.dif<font size=\"1\">group 1</font>] − [Mean.dif\r\n\r\n<font size=\"1\">group 2</font> /SD.dif<font size=\"1\">group 2</font>]</div><div><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;clear:both\"><br>where Mean.dif is the difference between the means of pre- and post-tests of each group and SD.dif is the standard deviation of the difference scores for each of the two independent groups.</p>I was wondering how to obtain SE of this effect size via lavaan using <a href=\"https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/256053/variance-of-cohens-d-for-within-subjects-designs/258583#258583\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/256053/variance-of-cohens-d-for-within-subjects-designs/258583%23258583&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422446668000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Fj9GCIvnZyHPtRxdg-RUB\">Mike Cheung&#39;s approach</a>?</div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#274e13\"><b>Reza Norouzian</b></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"monospace\" color=\"#274e13\">Postdoctoral Research Associate | Lecturer</font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"monospace\" color=\"#274e13\">Second Language Acquisition &amp; Research Methods, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(39,78,19);font-family:monospace;font-size:small\">Ph.D.</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(39,78,19);font-family:monospace;letter-spacing:0.2px\">College of Education &amp; Human Development</span><span style=\"color:rgb(39,78,19);font-family:monospace;font-size:small\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(39,78,19);font-family:monospace;font-size:small\">Dep. of Teaching, Learning &amp; Culture | Texas A&amp;M University</span><br></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"monospace\" color=\"#274e13\">College Station, TX 77843</font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"monospace\" color=\"#274e13\">Google Scholar: <a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=5B09zr8AAAAJ&amp;hl=en\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://scholar.google.com/citations?user%3D5B09zr8AAAAJ%26hl%3Den&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422446668000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08rEM9v_vKxP_0Us9SzkqF\">HERE</a></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"monospace\" color=\"#274e13\">University Webpage: <a href=\"https://directory.education.tamu.edu/view.epl?nid=rnorouzian\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://directory.education.tamu.edu/view.epl?nid%3Drnorouzian&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422446668000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PZb_VQXmyuCKF0qP4Sq-U\">HERE</a></font><font face=\"monospace\" color=\"#0000ee\"><u></u></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"monospace\" color=\"#274e13\">Email: <a rel=\"nofollow\">rnoro...@tamu.edu</a></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"monospace\" color=\"#274e13\">Phone: <a href=\"tel:(979)%20422-7052\" value=\"+19794227052\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(979)-422-7052</a><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#274e13\"><div><b>Future researchers will be challenged not only on the basis of their substantive questions, but also on how they manage to answer those questions in a methodical manner.</b></div></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
    ]
