  {
   "id": "nXm9eRQhCwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2020-01-28T09:18:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: Standard error (SE) of difference between two independent gains via lavaan",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Internally standardizing (i.e., within each group separately) is problematic.  Suppose the pre-post difference is the same in both groups.  The group difference would be zero, and a standardized version of that effect (i.e., the group-by-time interaction) should also be zero.  But if group 1&#39;s SD.dif is smaller/larger than group 2&#39;s SD.dif, then the difference in (internally) standardized means would be nonzero.  Large differences in SD.dif between groups would make your effect appear large, even when there is no difference between groups.  </div><div><br></div><div>The only way standardization works is to use a common norm. So you should probably pool SD.dif as well.  Using the principle behind the method Mike described, you would need to allow for group sizes to differ when you calculate SD.dif_pooled (e.g., see the formula for pooled &quot;<i>s</i>&quot; under Cohen&#39;s <i>d</i>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Effect_size#Cohen&#39;s_d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Effect_size%23Cohen&#39;s_d&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422446669000&amp;usg=AOvVaw01T8h0QrdmD8mWiZYuLUub\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Effect_size#Cohen&#39;s_d</a> )</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422446669000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OPgKpZgmbxz8IoHDUj4Jh\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "4M6O4As6CwAJ",
